  "difficulty_level": "H3",
  "difficulty_reason": "After standard twisted pseudodifferential calculus, functional calculus and Egorov, the proof constructs a spectrally truncated periodic operator and proves its microlocal localizations are genuine pseudodifferential operators. It then averages observables while preserving a Landau eigenspace, and projects coherent states to produce nonzero Gaussian beams with quantified h^(1/2) squared L2 norm and orbit localization. These constructions, followed by same-energy superposition and diagonal extraction, realize every invariant measure below the critical energy; standard coherent-state existence alone is insufficient.",
